{
  "$meta": {
    "description": "A generated DeepZoom pyramid served by the viewer itself — no image server, no download, no credentials",
    "dimension": "data",
    "clientKey": "localhost"
  },
  /**
   * The zero-dependency deployment. Generate the pyramid once:
   *
   *     npm run fixtures:synthetic
   *     npm run up:dev -- synthetic
   *
   * `test/harness/slides/make-synthetic.mjs` writes a DeepZoom directory of PNGs
   * plus one XML descriptor. OpenSeadragon autodetects a `.dzi` from the URL, so
   * nothing else is needed — which is what makes this the deployment to reach
   * for first when something is broken and you need to know whether it is the
   * viewer or the data.
   *
   * The tile pattern is diagnostic rather than decorative: each tile is tinted
   * by (level, col, row) and carries an 8x8 red corner marker, so tiles rendered
   * transposed, off-by-one, or from the wrong level look obviously wrong instead
   * of merely different.
   *
   * Two details worth knowing:
   *
   *  - `core.server.staticRoots` has to opt the fixture directory in. Static
   *    serving resolves against an allowlist of roots, not "any path that
   *    exists" — that is what keeps `env/*.json` and `*.server.ts` unreachable —
   *    and `test/` is deliberately not a default root.
   *  - The protocol template is absolute rather than relative so the URL
   *    survives OpenSeadragon's own tile-URL derivation (`<name>.dzi` ->
   *    `<name>_files/`). `<% XOPAT_NODE_PORT %>` is substituted server-side, so
   *    the same fragment works on whatever port the server actually bound —
   *    including the floating port the test harness assigns per worker.
   *
   * The one data id it serves is `synthetic.dzi`. Open it with
   * `?slides=synthetic.dzi`, or through any session naming that id.
   */
  "core": {
    "client": {
      "localhost": {
        "slide_protocols": {
          "static": "`http://localhost:<% XOPAT_NODE_PORT:-9000 %>/test/fixtures/slides/generated/${data}`"
        },
        "default_background_protocol": "static",
        "default_visualization_protocol": "static"
      }
    },
    "server": {
      "staticRoots": ["test/fixtures/slides"]
    }
  }
}
